[3.958, "o", "$ cua --root <example-output>\\project with spaces describe item_lookup\r\n"]
[3.958, "o", "{\n  \"stdout\": \"Capability    item_lookup  (version 1)\\nStatus        DRAFT - not approved; it will not run unattended\\nPurpose       Look up an item and return its available quantity and name\\nApplication   Stockroom 1.0 (app family stockroom), web; starts at {tenant.base_url}/login\\nSurface needs accessibility_tree, geometry, fixed_viewport, locations, forms, screenshots (declared); this build can run it.\\nSide effects  none - it only reads. Safe to run again with the same inputs.\\nHuman needed  only if something goes wrong.\\nSession       starts from a fresh sign-on.\\n\\nInputs (the caller supplies these)\\n  item_code           text, required\\n\\nSign-in (resolved by the runner from the tenant's secret store; never shown, stored or logged)\\n  app_login           username, password from secret://{tenant.id}/inventory/clerk\\n\\nOutputs (returned on success)\\n  quantity            whole number, required\\n                      read from the \\\"Value\\\" column of the row with \\\"Available quantity\\\", as a whole number\\n                        else the cell to the right of \\\"Available quantity\\\"\\n                        else the cell at screen position (439, 328) - for reference only; not used unattended\\n  item_name           text, required\\n                      read from the \\\"Value\\\" column of the row with \\\"Item name\\\", as text\\n                        else the cell to the right of \\\"Item name\\\"\\n                        else the cell at screen position (439, 279) - for reference only; not used unattended\\n\\nSteps (each control is found by the first description that matches it exactly)\\n  1. login.username   Type the app_login username (secret) into the textbox named \\\"Username\\\".\\n                      found by: the textbox named \\\"Username\\\"  [role_name]\\n                        else the textbox at screen position (260, 144) - for reference only; not used unattended  [bbox]\\n                      then expects: the field holds what was typed\\n                      if it cannot be done: hand the live session to a person\\n  2. login.password   Type the app_login password (secret) into the textbox named \\\"Password\\\".\\n                      found by: the textbox named \\\"Password\\\"  [role_name]\\n                        else the textbox at screen position (260, 230) - for reference only; not used unattended  [bbox]\\n                      then expects: the field holds what was typed\\n                      if it cannot be done: hand the live session to a person\\n  3. login.submit     Click the button named \\\"Sign in\\\".\\n                      found by: the button named \\\"Sign in\\\"  [role_name]\\n                        else the button at screen position (260, 292) - for reference only; not used unattended  [bbox]\\n                        else its recorded picture (91x45 px, sha256 c937a54489aa), only with --vision, only if one clear match, never on a commit  [vision]\\n                      then expects: the screen is at /lookup\\n                      if it cannot be done: hand the live session to a person\\n                      CHECKPOINT cp.logged_in: the screen is at /lookup; a \\\"Stock lookup\\\" heading is shown\\n  4. lookup.item_code Type the caller's item_code into the textbox named \\\"Item code\\\".\\n                      found by: the textbox named \\\"Item code\\\"  [role_name]\\n                        else the textbox at screen position (260, 144) - for reference only; not used unattended  [bbox]\\n                      then expects: the field holds the caller's item_code\\n                      if it cannot be done: hand the live session to a person\\n  5. lookup.submit    Click the button named \\\"Look up item\\\".\\n                      found by: the button named \\\"Look up item\\\"  [role_name]\\n                        else the button at screen position (260, 206) - for reference only; not used unattended  [bbox]\\n                        else its recorded picture (141x45 px, sha256 c6b385679012), only with --vision, only if one clear match, never on a commit  [vision]\\n                      then expects: the screen is at /items/<value>\\n                      if it cannot be done: hand the live session to a person\\n                      CHECKPOINT cp.item_details: the screen is at /items/<value>; a \\\"Item details\\\" heading is shown; the caller's item_code is shown; a \\\"Stock levels\\\" heading is shown\\n  end                 CHECKPOINT cp.done: quantity has been read; item_name has been read\\n\\nHow it can end\\n  success             returns quantity, item_name\\n  NOT_FOUND           business outcome - after lookup.submit, if \\\"Item not found\\\" is shown\\n  AUTH_FAILED         failure - after login.submit, if \\\"Invalid inventory credentials\\\" is shown\\n  (any step)          failure - a control cannot be found, or found more than once, or a check does not hold\\n\\nHandled automatically (the run carries on)\\n  SESSION_EXPIRED     once past cp.logged_in, if the screen is at /login: relogin (login.username, login.password, login.submit), then restart from the last checkpoint passed\\n                      at most 1 per step and 2 per run; beyond that the run fails\\n\\nWhere it came from\\n  discovered in run run_01M4H8G181J4YW86MQ3Z1YEW0D by scripted (scripted), recorded 2026-10-09T21:18:23.126Z\\n  transcript sha256 6b0d360f83d55ae36df4a3169b8a076000489564be473921d4bf9e4df304b0ab (the transcript stays in evidence, not in this file)\\n  screen positions were measured at 1280x800; they are used only there\\n\\nReviewed as version 1 (content 22ddfd83f336). To approve exactly this: cua approve <example-output>/project with spaces/capabilities/item_lookup.json --by <your name>\\n\"\n}\r\n"]
[4.35, "o", "$ cua --root <example-output>\\project with spaces approve item_lookup --by example-reviewer (scripted)\r\n"]
[4.35, "o", "{\n  \"stdout\": \"cua approve: item_lookup version 1 is approved by example-reviewer (scripted) (<example-output>/project with spaces/capabilities/item_lookup.json)\\n\"\n}\r\n"]
[15.629, "o", "$ cua --root <example-output>\\project with spaces replay item_lookup --input item_code=SKU-002 --inject changed_screen --handoff --handoff-wait 0 --operator-url http://127.0.0.1:51687\r\n"]
